Now we create the Share folder with PowerShell Admin.  

# 1. Create the physical folder on the C drive with your preferred name
New-Item -Path "C:\Network Share" -ItemType Directory -Force

# 2. Create the network SMB share with the exact same name
New-SmbShare -Name "Network Share" -Path "C:\Network Share" -FullAccess "Everyone"

# 3. Ensure the Windows Firewall allows File Sharing over the Private network profile
Enable-NetFirewallRule -DisplayGroup "File and Printer Sharing" -Profile Private  


What This Just Did

• Physically: You now have a folder located at C:\Network Share on that computer's drive.
• Logically: It is now being broadcast to your home network under the name Network Share.


Step 1: Map the Share via the Client's Command Line

Open a standard Command Prompt or PowerShell window on your client machine and run the following command to map the share to an available drive letter (we will use Z: as an example):
cmd
net use Z: "\\2603:6011:3701:fe0d:9ba:5684:9303:a4dd\Network Share"

